WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.280
One of the reasons that The Office became such&nbsp;
a big hit and beloved pop culture staple is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:11.200
the show's incredible ensemble cast. Against the&nbsp;
dullest possible backdrop — a mid-sized, somewhat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:17.040
unsuccessful paper company called Dunder Mifflin&nbsp;
located in "scenic" Scranton, Pennsylvania — The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.280
Office flourished because of characters&nbsp;
that viewers simply couldn't get enough of.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.880
Besides series star Steve Carell, who shepherded&nbsp;
Dunder Mifflin for seven seasons as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.400
well-meaning but occasionally clueless regional&nbsp;
manager Michael Scott, plenty of popular actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.240
spent time in Scranton — including Jack Ryan and&nbsp;
A Quiet Place star John Krasinski as Jim Halpert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.360
The Hangover breakout Ed Helms as Andy Bernard,&nbsp;
and The Mindy Project writer-showrunner Mindy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.920
Kaling as Kelly Kapoor. But let's not forget&nbsp;
about some of the other people who rose to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.960
stardom during their time on The Office —&nbsp;
like Phyllis Smith, who played Phyllis Vance.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.680
Smith wasn't even an actress before she was cast&nbsp;
on The Office, and many of her co-stars remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.560
her humble beginnings. During an episode of&nbsp;
their Office-themed podcast Office Ladies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.280
Angela Kinsey, who played Angela Martin, and&nbsp;
Jenna Fischer, who played Pam Beesly-Halpert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.400
talked about the fascinating&nbsp;
way they first met Smith.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.120
While discussing the show's start, Fischer mused…

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.880
"I think this is an interesting tidbit.&nbsp;
Phyllis Smith, who plays Phyllis on the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.120
she was the casting associate for The Office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.880
So when I auditioned for The Office,&nbsp;
she read my audition scenes with me."

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.760
Apparently, the pilot's director Ken Kwapis&nbsp;
particularly liked Smith after watching her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.320
read with the rest of the cast. Kwapis then&nbsp;
told Greg Daniels, who developed The Office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.000
that he wanted her on the show and&nbsp;
asked if he could give her a part.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.360
Fischer further explained,

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.080
"And so Phyllis went from&nbsp;
being a casting associate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.400
which she had done for years with Allison&nbsp;
Jones, [...] to having a part on this pilot."

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.240
Even though Fischer noted that Smith's&nbsp;
casting came with pretty low stakes — since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.160
they weren't sure the show would even&nbsp;
continue past its short first season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.400
it didn't seem like a problem for Smith to take&nbsp;
the part — but it's a good thing that she did, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.760
Phyllis Vance proved to be a fan favorite and one&nbsp;
of the most relatable characters on The Office.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.400
Phyllis' persona on the show was characterized&nbsp;
by her friendships with her co-workers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.880
a penchant for gossip and an extraordinarily&nbsp;
passionate relationship with her husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.200
Bob Vance of Vance Refrigeration.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.320
"We have a gym at home, it's called the bedroom."

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.240
While some of the other original cast&nbsp;
members left the show during its long run,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.760
Smith stuck with The Office until the very end&nbsp;
of the series in 2013. Although she's not on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.880
hit comedy anymore, Smith has branched out and&nbsp;
lent her talents to some seriously big projects.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.200
After several supporting roles in films&nbsp;
and TV shows during and after The Office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.400
including Butter, Bad Teacher, and Trophy Wife,&nbsp;
Smith accepted her biggest role when she signed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:46.480
on to one of Pixar's most ambitious projects:&nbsp;
2015's Inside Out. The film – which ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.920
won an Academy Award for Best Animated Feature —&nbsp;
featured Smith, her Office co-star Mindy Kaling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.280
Lewis Black, Bill Hader, and Amy Poehler as the&nbsp;
core emotions within the mind of an 11-year-old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:03.440
girl named Riley. Smith, with her kind and gentle&nbsp;
voice, perfectly embodied the character Sadness.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.680
"Crying helps me slow down and obsess&nbsp;
over the weight of life's problems."

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.480
Inside Out was a huge hit both critically&nbsp;
and commercially, and though Smith wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.480
seen on screen, her performance was&nbsp;
still familiar to fans of The Office.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:21.200
After Inside Out, Smith laid low for a few more&nbsp;
years before joining the streaming revolution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:27.120
and taking a role on Netflix's The OA, which ran&nbsp;
for two seasons before it was canceled in 2019.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:31.920
Alongside The OA creator and star Brit&nbsp;
Marling, Smith played Betty Broderick Allen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:37.040
often referred to as B.B.A., who works as&nbsp;
a schoolteacher. Together, Smith's B.B.A.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.040
and Marling's Prairie Johnson try to&nbsp;
uncover the secrets of the universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.960
Thanks to Smith's background as a dancer,&nbsp;
it turned out she was a perfect fit for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:50.480
this fantastical, unnerving, and creative show,&nbsp;
which introduced audiences to "the Movements."

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:56.320
Then in 2021, Smith landed a part in the Kristen&nbsp;
Wiig film Barb and Star Go to Vista Del Mar.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.520
While Smith is sure to have plenty&nbsp;
more career highlights in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.960
many fans will always think of&nbsp;
her as Phyllis from The Office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.480
and they'll remember her time on&nbsp;
the show with one thought in mind.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.000
"It was awesome."

